/-!
# KFC base: fine-cost item-language loops

Item-language (`IStmt`) building blocks whose per-element cost is `O(1 + zsz a)` for the moved
entry `a`, with **no** binary loop counter per element:

* `mvW X Y`   : move integers from `X` to `Y` until the top of `X` is not an integer
                (delimiter-driven, cost `(76 w + 131)` per entry of bit size `≤ w`);
* `uloop C D b`: run `b` once per mark on the *unary counter* `C` (the marks are moved to `D`
                and then moved back, so the counter is restored); overhead `64` per iteration;
* `mvB X Y C D`: move exactly `n` integers, `n` = number of marks on `C`;
* `toU A X K K2`: push `n` marks on `X`, where `n ≥ 0` is the integer on top of `A`
                (binary counter, cost `O((n+1)(zsz n + 2))`; superseded by the linear
                `KFCUnary.toUL`, which the programs use);
* `clrM X`    : drop all marks on top of `X`.
-/

